### Lesson Feedback API Tests

Exercises both feedback steps, the locked ratings and the summary with the
VS Code REST Client. See docs/lesson-feedback-architecture.md.

Select the `local` or `deployed` environment. `baseUrl`, `adminUid`,
`adminPassword`, `studentUid` and `studentPassword` are the variables
`grading.http` uses. Set them in the Git-ignored `.vscode/settings.json`.

Run the requests in order. They work on a throwaway "[TEST]" assignment made
in step 2. It is not team-taught (only the Pages sync bot sets teamTeach), so
its homework doesn't wait for this feedback. Logging in again replaces the JWT
cookie, so each "Sign in" switches who the requests run as.

### 1. Sign in as the teacher

POST {{baseUrl}}/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "uid": "{{adminUid}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### 2. Make a throwaway test assignment

# @name testAssignment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/assignments/test

### 3. Sign in as the student

POST {{baseUrl}}/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "uid": "{{studentUid}}",
  "password": "{{studentPassword}}"
}

### 4. Read your feedback before saving -> 200, every field null

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/lesson-feedback/{{testAssignment.response.body.$.id}}/mine

### 5. Save the lesson step with two ratings -> 200, lesson and popcorn locked

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/lesson-feedback/{{testAssignment.response.body.$.id}}/lesson
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lesson": 4,
  "popcorn": 3,
  "pros": "Clear examples"
}

### 6. Try to change a saved rating -> 409

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/lesson-feedback/{{testAssignment.response.body.$.id}}/lesson
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lesson": 5
}

### 7. Submission step without Grows -> 400 naming engage, homework and grows

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/lesson-feedback/{{testAssignment.response.body.$.id}}/submission
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "homework": 2
}

### 8. Complete the submission step -> 200, complete is true

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/lesson-feedback/{{testAssignment.response.body.$.id}}/submission
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lesson": 4,
  "engage": 5,
  "popcorn": 3,
  "homework": 2,
  "grows": "Slow down on the hacks"
}

### 9. A student can't read the summary -> 403

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/lesson-feedback/{{testAssignment.response.body.$.id}}/summary

### 10. Sign in as the teacher again

POST {{baseUrl}}/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "uid": "{{adminUid}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### 11. Live summary -> 200, responseCount 1, averages, counts and the comments

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/lesson-feedback/{{testAssignment.response.body.$.id}}/summary

### 12. Close the test assignment

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/assignments/{{testAssignment.response.body.$.id}}/close

### 13. Feedback is final after close -> 409

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/lesson-feedback/{{testAssignment.response.body.$.id}}/lesson
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pros": "Too late"
}
